From 57fdbb75ad958ab23712bd4fbcd4e9ae6c3b5420 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:30:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(security): security-only patch for production ff2f7da
 (next 16.4.3, sharp 0.35.5, zod 4.6.7)

Option A of the K-18 release plan: close the advisories that affect the
live site without the K-17 schema migration.

- next 16.3.6 -> 16.4.3 (GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw, GHSA-673q-mjm6-r5xr,
  GHSA-p3m5-59mp-jv5r), sharp 0.35.4 -> 0.35.5 (librsvg; the
  GHSA-2464 workaround), zod 4.6.5 -> 4.6.7 (GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5),
  source-map-js 1.2.1 -> 1.2.2. The lockfile changes only these
  packages and their platform binaries.
- media/processing.ts: file-signature check before sharp, identical to
  4aa0ae3 on the validation branch.
- tests/unit/security-patch.test.mjs: the SP tests from that branch
  (backup parts left out) plus a zod check.

No database calls or schema expectations change, so the code runs on
the live schema as it is. Local: npm audit (production) 0, typecheck,
ESLint 0 errors, unit 388/388, build 73/73. RLS/E2E need the CI database
job (not run: needs a push, which needs approval).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0148eusxoJiBurKT7xPz8Sh7
